From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nintendo-switch: boot the hekate L4T partition

hekate's installer marks no partition bootable. "bootflow scan" then looks at
partition 1 only, which is hekate's FAT32, so it never reaches
/boot/extlinux/extlinux.conf on the rootfs. hekate always puts L4T Linux on
partition 2. Try that partition by name first. Keep the scan as the fallback
for a card partitioned by hand.
---
--- a/configs/nintendo-switch_defconfig
+++ b/configs/nintendo-switch_defconfig
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 CONFIG_SYS_PBSIZE=2089
 CONFIG_SYS_PROMPT="Nintendo Switch # "
 CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=1
+CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="sysboot mmc 1:2 any ${scriptaddr} /boot/extlinux/extlinux.conf; bootflow scan"
 # CONFIG_BOOTM_PLAN9 is not set
 # CONFIG_BOOTM_RTEMS is not set
 # CONFIG_BOOTM_VXWORKS is not set
